# Cold-path fan-in CI (P4-D2)

Phase 4 made product workspace packages **lazy** on web/API/guest cold paths (dynamic `import()`, no SYNC fan-in, finance loaders async). P4.5 recorded that as a **qualitative** import-graph SoT. **P4-D2** turns the invariant into a **fast numeric CI guard** so regressions (static product fan-in returning to generated entrypoints) fail in seconds — without a full Next webpack analyzer on every PR.

## Problem

Qualitative before/after tables drift unless enforced. A future codegen change can reintroduce:

```ts
import { getDenaliWorkspacePlugin } from "@app-tour/workspace-denali/plugin";
```

at module eval of loaders/registries/finance bindings. That restores **O(N)** product packages on every boot, undoing P4.1–P4.2 / P4-D3.

Full `@next/bundle-analyzer` HTML reports need a production build (~minutes) and are a poor default PR gate under the Development Speed Protocol.

## Decision

| Layer | Role | Runtime |
| ----- | ---- | ------- |
| **`pnpm run guard:p4-cold-path-fan-in`** | **CI SoT** — static analysis of cold-path generated entrypoints | Target &lt; 5s |
| **Numeric report** | `reports/p4-cold-path-fan-in.json` — per-file static/dynamic product import counts | Written on each guard run |
| **Next bundle analyzer** | **Optional local** only — not wired as default CI | Full `pnpm --filter @apps/web build` with `ANALYZE=1` after installing `@next/bundle-analyzer` |

### Budget

For every file in the cold-path allowlist:

- **`staticProductImports === 0`** — no value `import … from "@app-tour/workspace-<product>[/…]"` ( `import type` from `@app-tour/workspace-sdk` remains allowed).
- **Dynamic** `import("@app-tour/workspace-…")` counts are **informational** (and must be ≥ product trunk size on web loaders + API registry).

Product package list comes from the generated allowlist fragment (`PRODUCT_WORKSPACE_PACKAGES`) so trunk growth updates the budget automatically after `generate:workspace-registry`.

### Cold-path allowlist (generated entrypoints)

| Surface | Path |
| ------- | ---- |
| Web plugin loaders | `apps/web/src/bootstrap/workspace-plugin-loaders.generated.ts` |
| Web admin themes | `apps/web/src/bootstrap/workspace-theme-stylesheets.generated.ts` |
| Web finance ops/nav | *(retired — capability registries; not cold-path generated)* |
| API plugin registry | `apps/api/src/workspace/workspace-plugin-registry.generated.ts` |
| API HTTP handlers | `apps/api/src/http/workspace-http-handler-loaders.generated.ts` |
| API finance\* | `apps/api/src/workspace-finance/workspace-finance-*-bindings.generated.ts` (+ capabilities) |
| Guest register router | `packages/guest-workspace-runtime/src/workspace-plugin-register-manifest.generated.ts` |
| Guest per-plugin registrars | `packages/guest-workspace-runtime/src/register-*.generated.ts` |
| Guest theme loaders | `packages/guest-workspace-runtime/src/workspace-guest-theme-stylesheets.*.generated.ts` |

\*Finance nav bindings are id-set only (no product imports) — included for completeness.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  subgraph cold [Cold module eval]
    L[web loaders]
    R[API registry]
    F[finance generated]
    G[guest register manifest]
  end
  subgraph hot [First resolve / request]
    D["await import(workspace-*)"]
  end
  Guard[guard:p4-cold-path-fan-in] -->|static count must be 0| cold
  cold -->|0 product packages| HotPath[process ready]
  HotPath --> D
```

## Out of scope

- Collapsing portal/marketing `package.json` product deps (P4.3 / P5 guest-runtime — already closed for registration ownership).
- Forcing HTTP handler loaders to per-id lazy (still one function with sequential `await import` — no **static** fan-in; residual scale ticket if needed).
- Adding `@next/bundle-analyzer` as a monorepo dependency or PR required check.

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run guard:p4-cold-path-fan-in
# optional unit:
node --test scripts/test/p4-cold-path-fan-in.spec.mjs
```

